    <div class="wb-head">
      <div class="wb-head-main">
        <h1>Tools for AI agents <span class="wb-chip">MCP · llms.txt · URL</span></h1>
        <p class="wb-about">The catalog currently has <strong>{{ stats.liveTools }} live tool pages</strong>, the MCP registry exposes <strong>{{ stats.mcpTools }} callable tools</strong>, and <strong>{{ stats.urlInvocableTools }} pages</strong> declare the documented URL-input/result contract. Routes are labelled browser, edge worker, direct network, or selectable AI. These integrations are experimental, so inspect the descriptor and route before relying on one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="wb-agents">
      <article class="wb-agent-card">
        <div class="wb-agent-n">01</div>
        <h2>Connect via MCP</h2>
        <p>Add Penumbra Forge as a Model Context Protocol server and your agent (Claude Code, Cursor, Claude Desktop, or another MCP client) gets non-model utility functions — hash, HMAC, base64/hex/url, JWT decode, UUID, entropy, CIDR, and others. The list below is what's exposed today.</p>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">local — runs on your machine <span class="wb-badge wb-badge--local">local process</span></div>
          <pre data-copy><span class="hl-dim"># server process is local; net-labelled tools still contact their documented destinations</span>
claude mcp add penumbra -- node ./workers/mcp/local.mjs</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">remote — hosted edge worker <span class="wb-badge wb-badge--local">live</span></div>
          <pre data-copy>claude mcp add --transport http penumbra https://penumbra-mcp.penumbraforge.workers.dev</pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="wb-agent-card">
        <div class="wb-agent-n">02</div>
        <h2>Discover via llms.txt</h2>
        <p>Tell your agent to read <a href="/llms.txt"><code>penumbraforge.com/llms.txt</code></a> — a machine-readable catalog listing every live page and an invocation example only where that page opts in. The full JSON index is at <a href="/tools/index.json"><code>/tools/index.json</code></a>.</p>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">agent prompt</div>
          <pre data-copy>Read https://penumbraforge.com/llms.txt and use the tools there.</pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="wb-agent-card">
        <div class="wb-agent-n">03</div>
        <h2>Invoke a tool by URL</h2>
        <p>Only catalog entries with an <code>invoke</code> descriptor promise automatic input and a machine-readable result. Put inputs in the URL fragment so they are processed by the page without being sent in the HTTP request. A browser-using agent navigates to the URL, waits for the ready marker, and reads the result.</p>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">navigate to an opted-in tool</div>
          <pre data-copy>https://penumbraforge.com/tools/hash-generator/#in=hello&amp;algo=SHA-256</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="wb-panel">
          <div class="wb-panel-bar">read the result (after html[data-pf-ready="1"])</div>
          <pre>document.querySelector('#pf-result').textContent   <span class="hl-dim">// JSON</span>
window.PF_RESULT   <span class="hl-dim">// { tool, ok, output, data }</span></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <div class="wb-note">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M12 2L3 7v6c0 5.25 3.75 10.1 9 11 5.25-.9 9-5.75 9-11V7l-9-5z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg>
      <p><strong>Fragments are the privacy-preserving default.</strong> Legacy <code>?in=</code> query links still work for compatibility, but queries reach the site/CDN and may appear in ordinary request logs before browser JavaScript runs. A <code>#in=</code> fragment is not included in the HTTP request.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="wb-related">
      <div class="wb-related-label">Tools currently exposed over MCP</div>
      <div class="wb-mcp-grid" id="mcpGrid"></div>
    </section>

    <div class="wb-note">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><path d="M12 2L3 7v6c0 5.25 3.75 10.1 9 11 5.25-.9 9-5.75 9-11V7l-9-5z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg>
      <p><strong>Where your input goes.</strong> The local MCP process handles non-model utility functions on your machine; tools marked <code>net</code> contact their documented destinations. The hosted MCP worker receives tool arguments and may be covered by ordinary hosting/security logs. Do not send sensitive input without checking the selected tool's route.</p>
    </div>
